¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxThus saith the Lord GOD; I will also make the multitude of Egypt to cease by the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°He and his people with him, the terrible of the nations, shall be brought to destroy the land: and they shall draw their swords against Egypt, and fill the land with the slain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼And I will make the rivers dry, and sell the land into the hand of the wicked: and I will make the land waste, and all that is therein, by the hand of strangers: I the LORD have spoken it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑThus saith the Lord GOD; I will also destroy the idols, and I will cause their images to cease out of Noph; and there shall be no more a prince of the land of Egypt: and I will put a fear in the land of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And I will make Pathros desolate, and will set fire in Zoan, and will execute judgments in No.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And I will pour my fury upon Sin, the strength of Egypt; and I will cut off the multitude of No.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And I will set fire in Egypt: Sin shall have great pain, and No shall be rent asunder, and Noph shall have distresses daily.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiThe young men of Aven and of Pi-beseth shall fall by the sword: and these cities shall go into captivity.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÜAt Tehaphnehes also the day shall be darkened, when I shall break there the yokes of Egypt: and the pomp of her strength shall cease in her: as for her, a cloud shall cover her, and her daughters shall go into captivity.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOThus will I execute judgments in Egypt: and they shall know that I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first month, in the seventh day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt; and, lo, it shall not be bound up to be healed, to put a roller to bind it, to make it strong to hold the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂTherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and will break his arms, the strong, and that which was broken; and I will cause the sword to fall out of his hand.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and put my sword in his hand: but I will break Pharaoh's arms, and he shall groan before him with the groanings of a deadly wounded man.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙûBut I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh shall fall down; and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall put my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall stretch it out upon the land of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and disperse them among the countries; and they shall know that I am the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse